  <result type="3">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Changes as a result of training</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopian donors interested in replicating training/workshop that Alert held at Dutch embassy in Ethiopia. Other donors working in Ethiopia recognise the importance of raising awareness among foreign investors operating in fragile context across Ethiopia and help them to not play into conflict dynamics with help of the CSBP approach. The workshop for other donors is likely to take place around in first half of 2020. (2020)
CS training for Dutch Embassy Ethiopia. 1. As a result of the training, the Embassy management and staff agreed to utilize the CS co-written by the Dutch MFA HQ and Alert. 2. There is a desire to align the conflict analysis requirements to the other analyses already captured in the HEAT mapping that the Embassy conducts (i.e. organizational analysis and context analysis). Those would help the teams consider conflict as its own category of risk and how the probability of conflict turning violent may impact the various activities that the team is already planning/currently implementing.(2021)
CS training for Dutch Embassy - Burkina Faso. At the end of the training, it was agreed that the embassy team would review their risk registers; update their conflict analysis with partners and review their indicators in their MEL frameworks. Given that this training was online, there has not been follow up to know what parts of this output has been delivered and/or led to what outcome/impact at this time.(2021)</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
